  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1137",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Liobagrus mediadiposalis Mori, 1936</li><li><strong>Common names:</strong> South Torrent Catfish, Jagasari (Korean)</li><li><strong>Type locality:</strong> Rakuto River at Bun-kei, Chosen, Korea.</li><li><strong>Pronunciation:</strong> lie oh BAG russ</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> 133 mm or 5.2 in SL.</li><li><strong>IUCN Red List category:</strong> Least Concern. Last assessed 2023.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1137",
      "html": "<p>Southern Asia: China, Japan and Korea waters.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1137",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.5 - 7.5</li><li>Temperature: 17.0-25.0°C (62.6-77°F)</li></ul><p>These fish reside in the temperate zone and undergo a wide range of temperatures throughout the year. They may tolerate higher and lower temperatures for a short period of time. Torrent-like conditions are not necessary, though the water should have some flow. The filter outflow is generally adequate.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1137",
      "html": "<p>There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1137",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: From the Greek, leios, meaning smooth, and bagrus, a name usually used for catfishes; in reference to the smooth head. Named after the genus Amblyceps, which refers to its blunt head.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
